model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Accounts and pool displays follow committed scoped revisions through the existing app-data supervisor transport. Hosted account, observation, link, group, role, sharing and session writers record revisions and pending delivery in their SQL transaction. Home readings and request history map to the actual pool app ID; derived usage, capacity, limit and price changes record their revisions and pending delivery with the Durable Object source commit. Identical writes and collection bookkeeping do not create revisions, and retry discovery adds no statement to unchanged pool upkeep. Registration precedes the authoritative handshake. A browser accepts a body only between matching current revision reads under one opaque principal/session identity, rejects older in-flight work, and clears protected data on denial. Hidden views do no data reads; reconnect compares durable heads and semantic expiry deadlines. Current accepted data remains visible only while an actual refresh is in flight or with its original observation and failure state. Unconverted app-version and generic-query reconciliation timers remain in place. Both hosted and self-hosted transports obey the same contract."
    }
  }
}
